<title>JAPAN: NTT, IBM agree to study network computing in Japan.</title>
<headline>NTT, IBM agree to study network computing in Japan.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Telegraph and Telephone Corp (NTT) and a Japanese unit of International Business Machines Corp (IBM) announced on Monday that they had reached an agreement to jointly study the network computing business in Japan.</p>
<p>The two companies said in a statement that they would hold a joint news conference on the details of their pact at 4 p.m. (0700 GMT) on Monday.</p>
</text>
